From: Peios Package Maintainers <packages@peios.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] clang: remove hmaptool's unused ctypes dependency

hmaptool imports ctypes.ArgumentError solely to reject a negative integer in
next_power_of_two().  It otherwise implements the header-map format with the
standard struct module.  Raise the ordinary built-in ValueError instead so the
tool and its tests work with Python builds that intentionally omit the optional
libffi-backed ctypes extension.

--- a/clang/utils/hmaptool/hmaptool
+++ b/clang/utils/hmaptool/hmaptool
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 #!/usr/bin/env python3
 from __future__ import absolute_import, division, print_function
 
-from ctypes import ArgumentError
 import json
 import optparse
 import os
@@ -136,7 +135,7 @@ def action_dump(name, args):
 
 def next_power_of_two(value):
     if value < 0:
-        raise ArgumentError
+        raise ValueError
     return 1 if value == 0 else 2**(value - 1).bit_length()
 
 def action_write(name, args):
